lazymidi 0.1.4 — upstream provenance

Adapted components (no upstream application is bundled):

1. Wooting Analog MIDI — e4e98975f56eb95be2f60bcedb0454c898479e74
   https://github.com/WootingKb/wooting-analog-midi
   Reference: wooting-analog-midi-core/src/lib.rs.
   Adaptation: velocity depth/time model, threshold/Shift semantics in
   crates/lazymidi-core/src/analog.rs. Added finite checks, latched releases,
   multiple bindings, resting/release velocity anchors, and optional
   installed-library lifecycle.
   The old src-tauri host is excluded because its MPL metadata differs from
   the root MIT license. No host, SDK Rust source, or SDK binaries are copied.

2. MIDI to QWERTY — 73e4d6bbcdbe154d90eaa9cd32a55ac16ddadb64
   https://github.com/ArijanJ/miditoqwerty-rs
   Reference: src native keyboard providers, key translations, and
   src/output_methods/pv.rs game/velocity mapping constants.
   Adaptation: physical scan-code/CoreGraphics translations in
   crates/lazymidi-core/src/platform/. Added HID identities, extended Windows
   scan codes, worker-owned handles, release ledgers, and structured errors.

3. pbek/LoopMidi — bc9cda9e6a29509996d9334ec8c6c14217beda5e
   https://github.com/pbek/loopmidi
   Functional reference only. Current source is GPL-3.0-only despite a stale
   README MIT statement. No source, translations, QML, or resources reused.
   lazymidi's step sequencer is independently implemented in Rust.

4. Wooting Analog SDK v0.9.1 — external installed dependency, MPL-2.0
   https://github.com/WootingKb/wooting-analog-sdk/tree/v0.9.1
   Not included in installers. ABI declarations independently expressed
   from the public C contract; the user supplies an installed library.

